<title>USA: Ultramar deal called defensive, strategically sound.</title>
<headline>Ultramar deal called defensive, strategically sound.</headline>
<byline>Brendan Intindola</byline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The merger of Diamond Shamrock Inc and Ultramar Corp would create a petroleum marketer and refiner with a strong regional presence in the U.S. and the bulk to ward off a hostile raid in an industry expected to see further consolidation.</p>
<p>Earlier, the companies announced an $850 million merger that calls for the conversion of each Diamond Shamrock share into 1.02 shares of Ultramar.</p>
</text>
